1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:01,740
She had a plan for the morning.

2
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:03,840
Then came an interruption.

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,560
Now, she’s trying to find her place again.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,760
“What was my next planned step?”

5
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:12,120
Threadline brings back her own note: “My
next planned

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,360
step is to water the plant by the window.”

7
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,700
A small reminder.

8
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,360
A place to begin again.

9
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,760
Another woman is looking back on the days
before her period.

10
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,540
“What helped me feel less rushed last time?”

11
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:27,880
She finds something she wrote herself:
leaving one evening free helped.

12
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,700
She can open that note, read it in context,

13
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:32,840
and add what she wants to remember this
time.

14
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:35,800
These are fictional examples from our early
prototype.

15
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:39,160
Threadline connects a question to the words
that came before it.

16
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,180
So you can pick up your thread.
